@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

# Variables captured dynamically from responses
@studentId = {{register.response.body.data.id}}
@authToken = {{login.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### ==================================================================
### 1. Root / Health Check Endpoint (Public)
### ==================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### ==================================================================
### 2. Authentication Flow (Public & Authenticated)
### ==================================================================

### 2.1 Register a New Student (POST)
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alex Johnson",
  "email": "alex.johnson@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

### 2.2 Login to Obtain JWT Bearer Token (POST)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alex.johnson@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

### 2.3 Get Current Authenticated User Profile (GET)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 2.4 Logout (POST)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### ==================================================================
### 3. Student Resource Endpoints (Protected by Bearer Token)
### ==================================================================

### 3.1 Get All Students (Paginated & Sorted)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/students?page=0&size=5&sort=name,asc
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 3.2 Get Student By ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/students/{{studentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 3.3 Update Student (Full Update - PUT)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/students/{{studentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alex Johnson Updated",
  "email": "alex.johnson@example.com"
}

### 3.4 Patch Student (Partial Update - PATCH)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/students/{{studentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alex Johnson Patched"
}

### ==================================================================
### 4. Error Handling & Validation Scenarios (RFC 9457 Testing)
### ==================================================================

### 4.1 Validation Error - Invalid Registration Payload (HTTP 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "A",
  "email": "invalid-email-format",
  "password": "123"
}

### 4.2 Conflict Error - Duplicate Email Registration (HTTP 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate User",
  "email": "alex.johnson@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

### 4.3 Unauthorized Error - Bad Login Credentials (HTTP 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alex.johnson@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword123!"
}

### 4.4 Unauthorized Error - Missing JWT Token (HTTP 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/students

### 4.5 Type Mismatch Error - Malformed UUID Path Variable (HTTP 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/students/invalid-uuid-format
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 4.6 Resource Not Found Error - Non-existent UUID (HTTP 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/students/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### ==================================================================
### 5. Cleanup - Delete Student (DELETE)
### ==================================================================

### 5.1 Delete Student By ID
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/students/{{studentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}